a. In acidic medium:
The oxidizing reactions of KMnO&lt;sub&gt;4&lt;/sub&gt; in acidic medium
i. Oxidation of iodide to iodine:
2MnO_4^{\ominus} + 10 I^{\ominus} + 16H^{\oplus} \longrightarrow 2Mn^{2\oplus} + 8H_2O + 5I_2
ii. Oxidation of Fe&lt;sup&gt;2 &lt;/sup&gt; to Fe&lt;sup&gt;3 &lt;/sup&gt;
\mathrm{MnO_4^{\,\ominus}} + 5\mathrm{Fe^{2\oplus}} + 8\mathrm{H^{\oplus}} \longrightarrow 5\mathrm{Fe^{3\oplus}} + \mathrm{Mn^{2\oplus}} + 4\mathrm{H_2O}
iii. Oxidation of H&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;S
H_2S \longrightarrow 2H^{\oplus} + S^{2\ominus}

5S^{2\ominus} + 2MnO_4^{\ominus} + 16H^{\oplus} \longrightarrow 2Mn^{2\oplus} + 5S + 8H_2O
iv. Oxidation of oxalic acid:
2MnO_4^{\ominus} + 5H_2C_2O_4 + 6H^{\oplus} \longrightarrow 2Mn^{2\oplus} + 10CO_2 + 8H_2O
b. In neutral or weakly alkaline medium:
i. Oxidation of iodide I^{\Theta} to iodate IO_3^{\Theta}.
2MnO_4^{\Theta} + H_2O + I^{\Theta} \longrightarrow 2MnO_2 + 2OH^{\Theta} + IO_3^{\Theta}
ii. Thiosulphate (S_2O_3^{\ 2\Theta}) is oxidised to sulphate (SO_4^{\ 2\Theta})
8MnO_4^{\Theta} + 3S_2O_3^{2\Theta} + H_2O \longrightarrow 8MnO_2 + 6SO_4^{2\Theta} + 2OH^{\Theta}
iii. Manganous salt is oxidised to MnO&lt;sub&gt;2&lt;/sub&gt;.
2MnO_4^{\ominus} + 3Mn^{2\oplus} + 2H_2O \longrightarrow 5MnO_2 + 4H^{\oplus}
